@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:architecture;desktop] mila-linux-single-instance
The application MUST use one stable GApplication id and HANDLES_OPEN activation so a second
launch forwards every `overalls://` URI to the existing process instead of creating another window.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;navigation] mila-linux-links-navigate-only
An accepted `overalls://` URI MUST select a typed navigation target only; activation MUST NOT issue a
runtime command, change a deployment, approve a session, or add credentials.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;protocol] mila-linux-route-closed-table
URI parsing MUST enforce the bounded closed route table and reject malformed authorities, unknown
paths, fragments, userinfo, encoded path segments, and non-canonical identifiers.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;architecture] mila-linux-typed-runtime-boundary
The native UI/runtime seam MUST exchange typed request and response values through a Rust trait;
raw pointers, credentials, authentication tokens, and terminal bytes MUST NOT appear in its API or
be logged by the scaffold.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;terminal] linux-terminal-renderer-bounded
The Linux terminal renderer MUST accept only decoded display text, reject unsupported control
characters and oversized chunks, and retain at most its configured viewport; terminal bytes MUST
remain owned by the authenticated transport and MUST NOT be logged or exposed to GTK state.


@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;navigation] linux-open-activation-batch
A desktop open activation MUST retain only the bounded set of parsed navigation routes; malformed
or excess URIs MUST become a count and MUST NOT be echoed, executed, or persisted.


@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;desktop] linux-machine-view-bounded
Machine list and detail labels MUST be derived from the validated authenticated listing, reject
control characters before GTK display, and expose permissions only as presentation hints.


@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;terminal] linux-terminal-transport-authenticated
The Linux PTY seam MUST require an authenticated session before attach, bind all operations to the
current generation, validate input and resize permissions, and keep PTY bytes outside GTK state.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security;web] linux-web-browser-fence
The GTK web action MUST launch only a Rust-validated public HTTPS endpoint whose
port matches the authenticated projection; private, stale, malformed, or
non-matching destinations MUST be refused before invoking the desktop browser.
